<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Display device configuration for y2q (Galaxy S20+ 5G, SM-G9860).

    <screenBrightnessMap> is REQUIRED by the schema:
    frameworks/base/services/core/xsd/display-device-config/display-device-config.xsd
    declares element "screenBrightnessMap" (type "nitsMap") with no minOccurs="0".
    Omitting it silently costs us auto-brightness:

      DisplayDeviceConfig.loadBrightnessMap()
        config.getScreenBrightnessMap() == null, so it falls back to
        loadBrightnessMapFromConfigXml(), which reads
        config_screenBrightnessNits / config_screenBrightnessBacklight.  Both are
        EMPTY on this device, so mNits and mBacklight stay null and
        BrightnessMappingStrategy.create() returns null, leaving
        DisplayPowerController with mUseSoftwareAutoBrightnessConfig = false.

    This map is the backlight <-> nits relationship the framework uses for both the
    brightness slider and the auto-brightness target conversion.  The values below
    are the effective curve of the earlier y2q tree, which is what the slider felt
    right on.  Two things were wrong with the r8q-inherited curve that this
    replaces, and both were visible symptoms:

      * It had plateaus and a 1.69x step between 249 nits (slider 0.60) and
        420 nits (slider 0.667) - "the first 60% only gets dimmer slowly, the last
        40% jumps".
      * Its bottom end was 12 nits, which was reported as too dark.

    The curve here is rescaled to 20 .. 800 nits: 20 keeps the dimmest step
    readable, and 800 is the panel's top non-HBM luminance.  The largest single
    step is 1.49x.

    interpolation="linear": this is a lookup table, and a monotone cubic spline
    would overshoot where the steps are uneven.  convertInterpolationType()
    (DDC.java:2887) accepts "linear".
-->
<displayConfiguration>
    <densityMapping>
        <density><height>3200</height><width>1440</width><density>600</density></density>
        <density><height>2400</height><width>1080</width><density>450</density></density>
        <density><height>1600</height><width>720</width><density>300</density></density>
    </densityMapping>

    <screenBrightnessMap interpolation="linear">
